background and terminations, and make the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"tracker’s records durable as the app leaves the foreground."}],"type":"topic","kind":"symbol","role":"collection","title":"LifecycleTracking"},"doc://Traffluent/documentation/Traffluent/TestingWhatYouTrack":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Traffluent\/documentation\/Traffluent\/TestingWhatYouTrack","title":"Testing What Your Code Tracks","type":"topic","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Run a test’s body with a fresh tracker and check the events it tracked."}],"kind":"article","role":"article","url":"\/documentation\/traffluent\/testingwhatyoutrack"},"doc://Traffluent/documentation/Traffluent/DefiningEvents":{"role":"article","type":"topic","title":"Defining Events","kind":"article","identifier":"doc:\/\/Traffluent\/documentation\/Traffluent\/DefiningEvents","url":"\/documentation\/traffluent\/definingevents","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Derive an event’s conformances and schema from its declaration with "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@Event"},{"type":"text","text":", and constrain which values its properties may hold."}]},"doc://MatomoEncoding/documentation/MatomoEncoding":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/MatomoEncoding\/documentation\/MatomoEncoding","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Send records to a Matomo installation as events, through its bulk tracking API."}],"type":"topic","kind":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/matomoencoding","role":"collection","title":"MatomoEncoding"},"doc://Traffluent/documentation/Traffluent/ChangingEvents":{"role":"article","type":"topic","title":"Changing an Event","kind":"article","abstract":[{"text":"An event’s version counts the changes that records stored before them can’t be read through, and only those. A compatible change keeps the version; a breaking one raises it.","type":"text"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/Traffluent\/documentation\/Traffluent\/ChangingEvents","url":"\/documentation\/traffluent\/changingevents"},"doc://CollectorEncoding/documentation/CollectorEncoding":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/CollectorEncoding\/documentation\/CollectorEncoding","url":"\/documentation\/collectorencoding","type":"topic","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Write batches of records in TraffluentCollector’s ingest format, for an "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"HTTPDestination"},{"type":"text","text":" to send,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"and read them back into records on a server."}],"kind":"symbol","role":"collection","title":"CollectorEncoding"},"doc://TracingDestinations/documentation/TracingDestinations":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/TracingDestinations\/documentation\/TracingDestinations","title":"TracingDestinations","type":"topic","abstract":[{"text":"A destination that adds each tracked event to the span that was active when it was tracked.","type":"text"}],"kind":"symbol","role":"collection","url":"\/documentation\/tracingdestinations"},"doc://Traffluent/documentation/Traffluent/TrackingEvents":{"role":"article","type":"topic","title":"Tracking Events","kind":"article","identifier":"doc:\/\/Traffluent\/documentation\/Traffluent\/TrackingEvents","url":"\/documentation\/traffluent\/trackingevents","abstract":[{"text":"Track typed events with a tracker, then deliver them in batches to any number of destinations.","type":"text"}]},"doc://Events/documentation/Events":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Events\/documentation\/Events","title":"Events","type":"topic","abstract":[{"text":"The types every other module shares: the ","type":"text"},{"code":"Event","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" protocol, the values its properties can hold, and the record a tracker makes of each event.","type":"text"}],"kind":"symbol","role":"collection","url":"\/documentation\/events"},"doc://Traffluent/documentation/Traffluent/SamplingEvents":{"role":"article","type":"topic","title":"Sampling Events","kind":"article","identifier":"doc:\/\/Traffluent\/documentation\/Traffluent\/SamplingEvents","url":"\/documentation\/traffluent\/samplingevents","ab